# CAD product / MCP namespace gate

This workspace is the **NYSDOT WZTC MicroStation** project. Live drawing work
uses **MicroStation CONNECT**, not AutoCAD.

## Hard rule

| Intent | Use | Do not use |
|--------|-----|------------|
| Live DGN / plan / callouts / views / place-edit | `user-wztc-designer` and/or `ms_connect` / bridge COM | `user-autocad` |
| AutoCAD / DWG only when engineer names it | `user-autocad` | — |

**Forbidden by default:** any `CallDynamicTool` / MCP call with namespace
`user-autocad` (including `capture_view`, `focus_view_on_elements`,
`describe_drawing_state`, place/edit tools).

## When AutoCAD is allowed

Only if the engineer **explicitly** says AutoCAD, DWG, or names an `.dwg`
path/session. Do not infer AutoCAD from overlapping tool names
(`capture_view`, `focus_view_on_elements`, etc.) — those exist on both
namespaces.

## Before the first live CAD tool call in a turn

1. Confirm product: MicroStation (default here) vs AutoCAD (opt-in).
2. Pick the matching namespace.
3. Confirm the **already-open** DGN/model is the one for the task. If not,
   **stop and ask** — never open/switch files (see `never-switch-dgn.mdc`).
4. If a MicroStation tool fails or returns empty handles, **debug MicroStation /
   COM / activated-ref** — do **not** fall back to `user-autocad`, and do
   **not** open another DGN.

## Incident (2026-09-10)

Agent used `user-autocad` mid MicroStation callout work; tools failed or
targeted the wrong product. Engineer called it out. This rule exists so that
does not recur.
